WEBVTT

00:16.975 --> 00:19.977
I am the man that chases
after the convenience store thief.

00:19.978 --> 00:21.688
The Crawler!

00:24.983 --> 00:27.193
Just leave that to the police.

00:27.777 --> 00:29.820
It’s dangerous to chase
after a motorcycle.

00:29.821 --> 00:32.364
<i>But I don’t want him to get away
by taking the backroads.</i>

00:32.365 --> 00:35.660
So, I’ll chase him
until the police arrive.

00:36.870 --> 00:38.371
QUIRK - LONGLEG

00:40.874 --> 00:41.916
Koichi!

00:45.628 --> 00:46.880
Ouch!

00:48.965 --> 00:51.425
Koichi, are you all right?

00:51.426 --> 00:52.635
Somewhat.

00:54.429 --> 00:57.556
Hey, you! You’re a pretty courageous boy!

00:57.557 --> 01:02.269
But you should leave the dangerous stuff
to the Pro Heroes!

01:02.270 --> 01:06.148
Yes, sir. I'm sorry. Thank you.

01:06.149 --> 01:07.858
Excuse me. What’s your name?

01:07.859 --> 01:11.820
What? How can this be?
You don’t know who I am?

01:11.821 --> 01:13.156
That’s ridiculous!

01:15.784 --> 01:19.162
I am America’s top ranking Hero,

01:19.662 --> 01:22.832
Captain Celebrity!

01:24.417 --> 01:26.293
I’ll give you my autograph.

01:26.294 --> 01:29.004
Make sure you remember my name.

01:29.005 --> 01:32.883
Hey, this is my All Might hoodie.

01:32.884 --> 01:35.177
Who cares about that?

01:35.178 --> 01:38.055
My signature is worth more.

01:38.056 --> 01:40.974
No, I think the worth of an object

01:40.975 --> 01:43.144
can only be determined by its owner.

01:44.813 --> 01:46.063
That was a funny joke.

01:46.064 --> 01:47.439
You got me with that.

01:47.440 --> 01:49.149
What did you say that was?

01:49.150 --> 01:50.734
All Might?

01:50.735 --> 01:53.946
If you ask me, he’s got strength
but not much else.

01:53.947 --> 01:56.908
He lacks elegance.

01:58.952 --> 02:00.078
Well, I’m off, Young Boy.

02:00.870 --> 02:02.914
Keep your make-believe Hero game
to a minimum.

03:38.801 --> 03:40.177
PROFESSIONAL

03:40.178 --> 03:41.428
A PERSON WHO DOES SOMETHING
AS A PROFESSION AND EARNS A LIVING

03:41.429 --> 03:42.638
ALSO, A WORK EXPERT OR SPECIALIST
WITH SPECIALIZED KNOWLEDGE

03:42.639 --> 03:43.932
AND SKILLS IN A SPECIFIC FIELD

04:24.389 --> 04:25.681
MR. CHRISTOPHER SKYLINE ARRIVES IN JAPAN

04:25.682 --> 04:28.767
<i>Mr. Christopher Skyline,
also known as Captain Celebrity,</i>

04:28.768 --> 04:32.437
<i>has announced that he will begin
his activities in Tokyo.</i>

04:32.438 --> 04:35.482
<i>What kind of ripple effect
will the arrival of this major class Hero</i>

04:35.483 --> 04:37.234
<i>from America cause in Japan's</i>

04:37.235 --> 04:40.488
- <i>hero industry?</i>
- Oh, he’s the one that saved Koichi.

04:40.989 --> 04:41.905
MR. CHRISTOPHER SKYLINE ARRIVES IN JAPAN

04:41.906 --> 04:44.366
<i>This footage shows the rescue scene
from the cruise ship accident</i>

04:44.367 --> 04:46.786
<i>off the coast of New York two years ago.</i>

04:47.287 --> 04:48.787
Wow, he’s pretty amazing.

04:48.788 --> 04:51.541
He’s got himself a good track record,
but he’s caused problems too.

04:52.125 --> 04:55.752
He’s also known
as Captain "Catastrophe" Celebrity.

04:55.753 --> 04:59.215
He's involved in a number
of lawsuits and scandals.

04:59.716 --> 05:01.466
He must’ve come to Japan to earn money,

05:01.467 --> 05:03.927
since he is no longer able to work
in his home country.

05:03.928 --> 05:07.598
I knew it.
I didn’t get a good vibe from him.

05:08.725 --> 05:11.560
It’s rare to hear you
badmouth someone, Koichi.

05:11.561 --> 05:14.272
He just rubs me the wrong way.

05:14.856 --> 05:17.858
Well, everyone has the right to decide
who they like or hate.

05:17.859 --> 05:20.110
By the way, what are you doing?

05:20.111 --> 05:23.281
I’m trying to clean my hoodie,
since he graffitied it.

05:51.392 --> 05:54.520
It’s a super gigantic Villain!

06:08.785 --> 06:11.329
He’s a straight up monster! A monster!

06:17.376 --> 06:18.669
"Gigantification", huh?

06:19.670 --> 06:22.297
The "Gigantification Quirk" is nice
because it’s really flashy,

06:22.298 --> 06:24.842
but it attracts the Heroes attention
too quickly.

06:25.635 --> 06:27.302
They get identified easily too,

06:27.303 --> 06:30.431
so they’re actually not that useful.

06:31.682 --> 06:35.394
I’ll just make sure
to extract samples from him later on.

06:36.395 --> 06:37.772
Good luck.

06:38.856 --> 06:42.610
Everyone! The monster is around 1-chome.

06:55.331 --> 06:58.250
Everyone, you still have time,

06:58.251 --> 07:00.627
so please remain calm and evacuate.

07:00.628 --> 07:02.212
No!

07:02.213 --> 07:05.423
- Masahiko is still inside the house!
- What?

07:05.424 --> 07:06.967
Hey, Young Boy,

07:06.968 --> 07:08.468
what’s the situation right now?

07:08.469 --> 07:11.138
Oh, Captain Celebrity. Great timing!

07:11.139 --> 07:14.434
It seems like a child was unable
to escape in time. We need to help him!

07:14.934 --> 07:18.229
Sorry, but can it wait a little?

07:18.729 --> 07:21.356
The media isn’t here yet,

07:21.357 --> 07:23.150
and my staff is still preparing.

07:23.151 --> 07:24.734
This is no time for that!

07:24.735 --> 07:28.280
First of all, we haven't received
a request from the police yet,

07:28.281 --> 07:30.992
so I'm not obligated to help out just yet.

07:31.492 --> 07:34.327
Forget you. I’m going on my own.

07:34.328 --> 07:35.871
Do as you like.

07:35.872 --> 07:39.082
<i>C.C. Captain Celebrity.</i>

07:39.083 --> 07:42.085
Oh, here it comes. This is C.C.

07:42.086 --> 07:45.380
We received a dispatch request
from the Naruhata Police Station.

07:45.381 --> 07:47.716
<i>Cooperation with the media outlets</i>

07:47.717 --> 07:49.676
<i>and teamwork with local Heroes
have been arranged.</i>

07:49.677 --> 07:53.848
<i>Staff members on the ground have confirmed
all the people in need of help.</i>

07:54.515 --> 07:56.057
I’m good to go too.

07:56.058 --> 07:57.643
I’m ready when you are.

08:33.679 --> 08:36.557
Hey, Masahiko-kun!

08:37.141 --> 08:38.267
Masahiko-kun!

08:42.271 --> 08:43.773
Masahiko-kun!

08:49.320 --> 08:50.905
Masahiko...

08:51.531 --> 08:52.990
is a dog?

08:54.825 --> 08:56.826
He’s a dog,
but his life is just as precious.

08:56.827 --> 08:58.037
MASAHIKO

08:58.704 --> 09:01.707
All right, let’s escape together,
Masahiko!

09:02.375 --> 09:05.293
It’s almost the grand finale!

09:05.294 --> 09:07.337
<i>This teetering super giant Villain</i>

09:07.338 --> 09:09.381
<i>receives a decisive blow</i>

09:09.382 --> 09:11.133
<i>from Captain!</i>

09:27.650 --> 09:31.319
<i>The Captain rescued someone
who was beneath the falling Villain!</i>

09:31.320 --> 09:33.447
<i>It seems to be a boy
who couldn’t escape in time!</i>

09:34.365 --> 09:37.784
<i>Quick and reliable! And very elegant!</i>

09:37.785 --> 09:38.869
<i>Not only that...</i>

09:39.870 --> 09:42.038
<i>As a kind gesture of fan service,</i>

09:42.039 --> 09:45.250
<i>he's giving the boy he rescued
an autograph as a gift!</i>

09:45.251 --> 09:48.878
<i>This is what America's top ranking Hero
is capable of.</i>

09:48.879 --> 09:54.927
<i>This is Captain Celebrity!</i>

09:57.013 --> 09:59.180
Apparently, while Captain was fighting,

09:59.181 --> 10:01.934
his team saved about 100 people.

10:02.518 --> 10:05.645
I guess I’m counted
as one of those 100 people?

10:05.646 --> 10:08.231
Well, that’s true...

10:08.232 --> 10:10.567
But it seems like no one
was seriously injured,

10:10.568 --> 10:12.861
so, all’s well that ends well, right?

10:12.862 --> 10:14.238
Masahiko!

10:17.908 --> 10:20.995
Thank you for saving Masahiko, Cruller.

10:22.330 --> 10:26.374
Pets are not within
our range of expertise,

10:26.375 --> 10:29.670
so, all the credit goes to you,
Young Boy, for saving that dog.

10:30.254 --> 10:32.881
Not too shabby, Young Man.

10:32.882 --> 10:34.883
Thanks.

10:34.884 --> 10:38.179
By the way, I have a favor to ask of you.

10:38.679 --> 10:42.766
Can you stop darting around
under my foot in that lame outfit?

10:42.767 --> 10:45.769
Once that weird hoodie appears
on the TV screen,

10:45.770 --> 10:48.730
the entire scene becomes really lame.

10:48.731 --> 10:49.898
After all,

10:49.899 --> 10:53.653
the footage of the crime scene
is also part of my personal image.

10:54.236 --> 10:56.155
Got it?

10:58.741 --> 11:01.160
Yeah, I hate that guy after all.

11:01.994 --> 11:04.914
NO TRESPASSING
DANGEROUS

11:15.174 --> 11:16.549
It’s about to collapse.

11:16.550 --> 11:20.136
It became even more fragile
after the monster incident this afternoon.

11:20.137 --> 11:22.305
Did everyone inside escape?

11:22.306 --> 11:24.558
They haven’t been able
to confirm that yet.

11:25.726 --> 11:27.395
- It's falling apart!
- Watch out!

11:31.440 --> 11:33.400
I'm the man who rescues people

11:33.401 --> 11:35.319
who are left behind
in a collapsing building!

11:36.737 --> 11:39.198
The Crawler!

11:41.409 --> 11:43.786
A sumo wrestler and a lady,
both with an injured leg!

11:45.246 --> 11:48.707
What should I do? I can’t carry
them both at the same time.

11:49.542 --> 11:50.542
Hey, Young Boy.

11:50.543 --> 11:51.918
Captain Celebrity!

11:51.919 --> 11:55.172
Seems like we’ll have to cooperate here.

11:58.509 --> 11:59.718
There’s someone coming out.

12:06.267 --> 12:10.145
Shouldn’t this be the other way around?

12:10.146 --> 12:11.855
No, this is just fine.

12:11.856 --> 12:16.152
Because I’m not interested
in carrying a man.

12:17.153 --> 12:20.447
It has nothing to do with your interests!

12:20.448 --> 12:21.532
Many thanks.

12:24.994 --> 12:26.245
Whoa!

12:27.538 --> 12:29.165
Rescue complete.

12:30.958 --> 12:34.252
Members of the press,
you may take photographs.

12:34.253 --> 12:37.088
He’s getting all the credit again.

12:37.089 --> 12:38.340
Many thanks.

12:38.966 --> 12:41.302
- Koichi!
- Many thanks.

12:42.470 --> 12:44.053
Now,

12:44.054 --> 12:47.140
we’ll demolish this dangerous building!

12:47.141 --> 12:49.101
Let’s all have fun with it!

13:11.248 --> 13:13.416
He brought along cheerleaders this time?

13:13.417 --> 13:16.044
Maybe this is the American way
of doing things?

13:16.045 --> 13:19.881
Heroes in Japan are treated
like celebrities too.

13:19.882 --> 13:23.344
Maybe it’s not so bad to put on
a big show after getting the job done.

13:24.595 --> 13:26.764
I can get tips for my own live shows.

13:29.683 --> 13:34.730
But I feel like this is a bit frivolous
and insensitive...

13:35.940 --> 13:37.316
He’s so flashy. I’m jealous.

13:37.900 --> 13:40.027
You just spilled the truth.

13:40.736 --> 13:44.656
The demolition is all complete.
Good work, everyone!

13:44.657 --> 13:47.367
That voice... Makoto-senpai!

13:47.368 --> 13:50.036
Let's take roll calls for each squad
and get ready to leave.

13:50.037 --> 13:50.955
Okay!

13:51.539 --> 13:55.918
I don’t like it that she’s cheering
for a guy like that.

13:57.086 --> 13:59.212
Plus, look at how vulgar that is.

13:59.213 --> 14:01.715
Jumping and bouncing around
in a miniskirt like that. How stupid.

14:03.384 --> 14:06.010
These are meant to be seen!

14:06.011 --> 14:08.305
Maybe those are meant to be seen too.

14:10.099 --> 14:11.516
Oh, it’s Cruller and Pop☆Step.

14:11.517 --> 14:12.934
I need to get an interview.

14:12.935 --> 14:15.395
Can you spare me a minute?

14:15.396 --> 14:16.730
Oh crap, she saw us.

14:18.899 --> 14:20.984
How are things, Makoto?

14:20.985 --> 14:22.652
Doing well, Boss.

14:22.653 --> 14:26.114
Please call me Chris.

14:26.115 --> 14:30.870
I’ve heard that you’re
a very capable leader.

14:31.579 --> 14:32.871
I just like being in charge.

14:32.872 --> 14:36.542
Oh, no need to be humble.
You've been a great help to me.

14:37.167 --> 14:40.628
I would like to communicate with you
more intimately

14:40.629 --> 14:41.880
for our future endeavors.

14:41.881 --> 14:45.842
In other words, I think we need
to get to know each other

14:45.843 --> 14:47.176
a lot better.

14:47.177 --> 14:50.680
I’m honored. Then,
let’s have lunch together next time.

14:50.681 --> 14:52.224
I’ll make a reservation.

14:53.392 --> 14:57.228
While you’re at it, make it a restaurant
on the top floor of a skyscraper.

14:57.229 --> 14:58.939
How lovely.

14:59.940 --> 15:03.401
He’s touching her shoulder.
What a pervert.

15:03.402 --> 15:08.115
That bastard. Seems like
his bad habits are coming back.

15:08.699 --> 15:09.575
Oh, Master.

15:12.077 --> 15:14.662
<i>Captain "Catastrophe" Celebrity,</i>

15:14.663 --> 15:16.957
<i>also known as "The Soaring Stallion".</i>

15:18.083 --> 15:21.669
<i>Most of the lawsuits he's facing
are related to women.</i>

15:21.670 --> 15:23.504
<i>The biggest one</i>

15:23.505 --> 15:26.592
<i>is the compensation demanded
from his currently estranged wife.</i>

15:27.176 --> 15:30.303
<i>He's still not deterred, even after
being stripped of everything he owns...</i>

15:30.304 --> 15:31.304
Well, now that

15:31.305 --> 15:35.434
he's out of his wife’s surveillance,
he feels free to spread out his wings.

15:36.018 --> 15:38.896
Either way, he hasn’t learned his lesson.

15:39.730 --> 15:43.609
SOME TIME LATER

15:46.320 --> 15:49.739
Now, he’s trying to sink
his poisonous fangs into Makoto-senpai.

15:49.740 --> 15:51.574
I can’t let that happen.

15:51.575 --> 15:53.826
Who cares? Leave her be.

15:53.827 --> 15:55.203
Hey, Young Boy,

15:55.204 --> 15:58.916
what are you doing trailing
after a girl from my office?

15:59.583 --> 16:02.293
Oh, Koichi-kun. What’s the matter?

16:02.294 --> 16:05.505
Oh, I just happened to see you,

16:05.506 --> 16:08.091
so I wanted to see what you were doing.

16:08.092 --> 16:10.468
He’s my junior at my university.

16:10.469 --> 16:12.929
Oh, you’re a student?

16:12.930 --> 16:16.224
Yes, I’m just an ordinary
university student.

16:16.225 --> 16:19.227
Makoto and I are going on a date now.

16:19.228 --> 16:20.938
It’s a work-related meeting.

16:21.522 --> 16:23.148
All right, let’s go.

16:25.317 --> 16:27.069
Damn it!

16:32.741 --> 16:33.575
Oh no,

16:34.410 --> 16:37.036
looks like there’s a bank robbery
happening nearby.

16:37.037 --> 16:39.331
Oh, forget that.

16:40.332 --> 16:43.460
This moment with you
is much more important.

16:45.546 --> 16:48.924
- Now, I’m getting a call.
- Just hang up.

16:49.925 --> 16:52.886
More importantly, I want to carry you,
soar across the sky,

16:53.595 --> 16:56.974
and take you somewhere
even more beautiful...

17:14.616 --> 17:17.493
She’s been personally
confiding in me and said,

17:17.494 --> 17:20.955
"If my husband reverts
to his bad habits while overseas,

17:20.956 --> 17:22.790
I will consider it as showing no remorse

17:22.791 --> 17:25.752
and use it as material
for another lawsuit."

17:25.753 --> 17:29.338
And your wife is asking, "What did
you mean by ‘I want to carry you’?"

17:29.339 --> 17:30.381
Excuse me.

17:30.382 --> 17:34.178
I think there’s an incident outside
I need to help out.

17:37.097 --> 17:39.265
Get the getaway car ready.

17:39.266 --> 17:42.311
An eco-friendly car that’s safe
for the environment.

17:43.687 --> 17:45.897
The perpetrator has barricaded himself
and has fired shots!

17:45.898 --> 17:49.067
It’s dangerous, so stand back. Stand back.

17:49.068 --> 17:52.153
I came out to do some shopping,
but there’s another incident?

17:52.154 --> 17:53.571
Oh man,

17:53.572 --> 17:55.740
I left my Exclusive All Might Hoodie
at home.

17:55.741 --> 17:59.202
The police are already here,
so there’s nothing for you to do.

17:59.203 --> 18:01.496
What were you going to do
if you had your hoodie?

18:01.497 --> 18:02.414
Here he is!

18:02.998 --> 18:04.625
Captain Celebrity.

18:10.297 --> 18:13.342
Stay away, Hero! I have hostages...

18:18.138 --> 18:20.264
- Chris!
- C.C!

18:20.265 --> 18:21.808
Sorry,

18:21.809 --> 18:24.937
I can’t be seen with girls right now.

18:29.483 --> 18:33.194
Young Boy, great timing!
Can you come with me for a second?

18:33.195 --> 18:34.530
Me?

18:36.365 --> 18:37.741
Koichi!

18:40.828 --> 18:43.579
Honey, did you see
the pictures I sent you?

18:43.580 --> 18:46.082
I think there's been
some misunderstanding,

18:46.083 --> 18:49.085
but it was just part
of fan service, that’s all.

18:49.086 --> 18:52.089
But something seems off with this picture.

18:52.673 --> 18:55.591
He really doesn’t have the image
of being buddy-buddy

18:55.592 --> 18:56.760
with other men.

18:57.261 --> 18:59.720
Gaining the support of men...

18:59.721 --> 19:02.098
Erasing the scandalous image...

19:02.099 --> 19:04.393
A new stage called Japan...

19:05.102 --> 19:05.935
That's right!

19:05.936 --> 19:08.647
Boss, now’s your chance
to change your image!

19:12.359 --> 19:14.944
<i>Captain Celebrity has been known</i>

19:14.945 --> 19:16.779
<i>as a Playboy Hero for many years,</i>

19:16.780 --> 19:20.409
<i>but it seems like he's now commercializing
a new concept since his arrival to Japan.</i>

19:20.909 --> 19:22.618
Hey-ya!

19:22.619 --> 19:23.619
LEFT HIS SEX APPEAL!
THIS IS TRUE STRENGTH!

19:23.620 --> 19:24.913
Hey-ya! Chris!

19:25.956 --> 19:27.583
Hey-ya! Chris!

19:28.208 --> 19:31.879
Fly! Fly! Fly, Chris!

19:32.504 --> 19:34.046
Hey-ya! Chris!

19:34.047 --> 19:36.424
LONE WOLF

19:36.425 --> 19:37.801
Hey-ya! Chris!

19:38.385 --> 19:42.055
<i>Look up at the sky</i>

19:42.973 --> 19:46.225
What the hell happened to him?

19:46.226 --> 19:48.186
Is he having an identity crisis?

19:48.187 --> 19:49.478
Who knows?

19:49.479 --> 19:54.775
It’s common for a foreign celebrity
to try out novel ideas.

19:54.776 --> 19:55.902
CAPTAIN CELEBRITY MAKING A BOLD CHANGE

19:55.903 --> 19:57.905
Hey-ya! Chris!

21:28.036 --> 21:28.911
SOME TIME LATER

21:28.912 --> 21:31.247
Hey, Dad. What is it all of a sudden?

21:31.248 --> 21:34.458
<i>Sorry, Koichi, but your mom...</i>

21:34.459 --> 21:35.668
What?

21:35.669 --> 21:37.545
Mom is coming here?

21:37.546 --> 21:40.298
She has a reunion here,
so she’s staying over at my place?

21:40.299 --> 21:41.799
She’s already on the train?

21:41.800 --> 21:44.260
Oh no, this is a crisis!

21:44.261 --> 21:46.053
Why are you panicking?

21:46.054 --> 21:48.597
My mother is a very strict person.

21:48.598 --> 21:50.141
If I'm slacking, she will scold me.

21:50.142 --> 21:53.312
Scold? You’re not a child anymore.

21:53.895 --> 21:55.772
You don’t know my mother.

21:56.356 --> 21:59.942
She was against me moving out here
to Tokyo in the first place.

21:59.943 --> 22:02.903
She said, "A good-natured person like you
will get tricked by bad people

22:02.904 --> 22:05.198
in the city and get involved in crime."

22:05.949 --> 22:07.867
She really believes that.

22:07.868 --> 22:09.785
<i>Wow, she was totally right.</i>

22:09.786 --> 22:11.370
That's why,

22:11.371 --> 22:14.332
if she thinks I’m doing anything wrong,
she’ll make me quit school,

22:14.333 --> 22:16.834
and she'll take me back
to the countryside.

22:16.835 --> 22:17.752
What?

22:17.753 --> 22:20.504
I’ve been giving her updates
over the phone.

22:20.505 --> 22:23.424
What did I tell her?

22:23.425 --> 22:26.886
"I’m doing well in school," "I'm being
recognized at my part-time job,"

22:26.887 --> 22:28.846
and "I'm living a fulfilling life."

22:28.847 --> 22:32.433
That sounds good. It’s mostly true.

22:32.434 --> 22:34.478
"I also found a lovely girlfriend."

22:35.771 --> 22:38.814
My mom hates lies.

22:38.815 --> 22:41.692
What should I do if she says,
"Introduce me to her."

22:41.693 --> 22:45.488
How would I know?
Why would you tell such a stupid lie?

22:45.489 --> 22:47.031
How should I say it?

22:47.032 --> 22:49.408
I kind of exaggerated things.

22:49.409 --> 22:51.202
You’re so stupid.

22:51.203 --> 22:52.788
I’m leaving.

23:02.756 --> 23:04.174
I’m here, Koichi!

23:04.758 --> 23:07.344
Hello. Long time no see, Mother.

23:10.430 --> 23:12.057
FOR GUESTS

23:14.601 --> 23:17.394
Seems like you’re doing rather well.

23:17.395 --> 23:18.480
Yes.

23:19.481 --> 23:22.483
Now, introduce me to your girlfriend.

23:22.484 --> 23:24.986
<i>Straight to the topic!</i>

23:26.571 --> 23:29.406
<i>Oh no, this is an emergency!
Mom is coming here!</i>

23:29.407 --> 23:33.077
<i>I have to show her that I'm living
a fulfilling life as a student in Tokyo!</i>

23:33.078 --> 23:35.830
<i>Otherwise, she'll drag me back
to the countryside!</i>

23:35.831 --> 23:37.581
<i>Next episode, "Mom Descends".</i>

23:37.582 --> 23:39.333
<i>What? You want to meet my girlfriend?</i>

23:39.334 --> 23:40.417
<i>You've got to be kidding me!</i>

23:40.418 --> 23:41.878
Subtitle translation by: Lili Morita
